              <tr>
                <td width="186" valign="top" class="row1" nowrap> <span class="largetext"><a name="14459"></a><b>Palewren</b></span><br />
                  <span class="smalltext">Extraplanar<br />
                  <img src="images/avatars/gallery/000-100/056.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
                  <br />
                  Joined: 29 Nov 2002<br />
                  Posts: 238<br />
                  </span><br>
                  <img src="templates/millenniumFalcon/images/spacer.gif" height="3"><br>
                  &nbsp;<a href="posting.php?mode=quote&amp;p=14459&amp;sid=a6cdb0acfcb657d7315d434490c8d22c"><img src="templates/millenniumFalcon/images/icon_quote_lang.gif" alt="Reply with quote" title="Reply with quote" border="0" /></a>&nbsp;&nbsp;
                  </td>
                <td valign="top" class="row2"> <span class="smalltext"><b></b></span>
                  <p><span class="largetext">Sorry I didn't check back.  Been busy at work and playing PS when I'm not here.
<br />

<br />
There is ZERO story.  well...
<br />
Blah blah blah explorers go thru wormhole.  Wormhole closes, explorers break off into 3 factions.  War ensues.  Alien technology = respawning (no permanent death)  
<br />

<br />
Everyone starts with 4 certification points.  No current skill costs more than 4 points.  Some have prereqs but none of those (combined with their prereq) cost more than 5 cert points.  You can get 2 battle ranks just trying out everything in the VR training at your home base (sanctuary).  Each level gives you 1 certification point.
<br />

<br />
Every 6th level (6,12,1<img src="images/smiles/icon_cool.gif" alt="icon_cool.gif" border="0" /> will get you one more implant slot.  These can be changed at any time at a proper station.  They are things like regen, see cloak, advanced targeting blah blah blah.
<br />

<br />
Certifications can be forgotten at a rate of once per 24 hours so you are never stuck permanently with a skill.  Certificates involve weapons, armor, mech suits, vehicles and skills (repair, healing, hacking).
<br />

<br />
The game is a giant capture the flag match with 3 teams.  It goes on round the clock as any mmorpg.  (think DAOC + Quake)  Or tribes if you played that.
<br />

<br />
Anyone with the proper tool (that mech suits can't use) can hack a base or tower.  Towers are staging points mostly and offer no exp but hack instantly once the hacking is actualy finished.  A base once hacked starts a 15min timer.  If the defending faction doesn't "resecure" (hack again) the base in the 15min it changes hands to the hackers faction.  This nets the bulk of your exp in the game.  700-5k compared to 1-50 or so from a normal kill.
<br />

<br />
Vehicles are very cool and damn near a requirement for getting around.  Drop ships are one of the choices as well as tanks, jets, APC's and the like.  Good to keep your group (squad up to 10 peeps) togeather.  If that fails every 10 min a HART (big orbital dropship) EQ boat will depart from your sanctuary.  From there you can drop anywhere in the game accept for right on top of a base or tower.
<br />

<br />
Weapons are typicaly anti infantry, anti air or anti vehicle.  One type tends to work very poorly against the others.  Sure you can blow up that tank with that gun but somehow a foot soldier can soak it up.  <img src="images/smiles/icon_wink.gif" alt="icon_wink.gif" border="0" />  Think rock paper siscors.
<br />

<br />
No money or items to farm.  It's jsut a matter of defending the proper dispensor terminal.  If you are certified to use something you can get it with few exceptions.  (Such as must control X type of facility on continent for Y vehicle type.)
<br />

<br />
If you enjoy FPS games I highly recomend this one.  A low level player is almost as effective as a max level (20) player.  They just have to be more focused in what they can do where a level 20 can do just about anything they want.<br />_________________<br /><a href="http://www.magelo.com/eq_view_profile.html?num=531009" target="_blank" class="postlink">Palewren Shadowcrest</a></span><span class="smalltext"></span></p>
